---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import TrustStrip from '../components/TrustStrip.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="What is Functional Medicine? | Dr. Harshitha Jain, Bengaluru"
  description="Understand functional medicine: an evidence-grounded systems-biology approach that uncovers the root physiological causes of chronic conditions in Bengaluru."
>
  <!-- Page Header -->
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container text-center">
      <span class="section-eyebrow">Patient Education</span>
      <h1 class="page-title">Medicine That Asks <em>Why</em>, Not Just <em>What</em></h1>
      <p class="lead" style="max-width: 720px; margin: var(--space-3) auto 0;">
        Functional medicine is an evidence-grounded, systems-biology approach that seeks to uncover and rebalance the upstream causes of chronic illness.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <TrustStrip />

  <!-- Explainer Section -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="explainer-grid">
        <div class="explainer-text">
          <span class="section-eyebrow">The Core Distinction</span>
          <h2>Beyond Symptom Suppression to Systems Biology</h2>

          <div class="explainer-paragraphs">
            <p>
              <strong>Conventional medicine is extraordinary</strong>—it excels at acute trauma, bacterial emergencies, emergency surgical procedures, and crisis management. When you have a broken bone, acute appendicitis, or a sudden severe infection, conventional hospital care is indispensable.
            </p>

            <p>
              However, modern chronic conditions—such as longstanding thyroid imbalances, persistent fatigue, irritable bowel habits, chronic sinus inflammation, and cyclical mood dips—behave differently. They rarely arise overnight from a single pathogen. Instead, they reflect a gradual accumulation of metabolic stress, dietary triggers, gut dysbiosis, hormonal shifts, and nervous system overload.
            </p>

            <p>
              <strong>Functional Medicine complements conventional care</strong> by mapping how different bodily systems interact. Rather than viewing the thyroid, the stomach, and the brain as disconnected silos, we investigate the shared biochemical pathways connecting them.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="explainer-image-box">
          <img 
            src="/images/holistic-science.jpg" 
            alt="Scientific botanical and biochemical nutrition elements representing functional medicine" 
            width="800" 
            height="500" 
            class="explainer-img"
          />
          <div class="image-caption">
            <p><strong>Science-Backed Nutrition & Biochemistry:</strong> Investigating cellular nutrient cofactors, gut barrier competence, and metabolic rhythms.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Side-by-Side Comparison Table (NMC Compliant) -->
  <section class="section comparison-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Two Complementary Modalities</span>
        <h2>How Both Approaches Work Together</h2>
        <p class="section-description">
          Functional medicine does not compete with conventional medicine; it deepens the investigation for complex, unresolved conditions.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="table-container card">
        <table class="comparison-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col" style="width: 28%;">Clinical Dimension</th>
              <th scope="col" style="width: 36%;">Conventional Medical Focus</th>
              <th scope="col" style="width: 36%;">Functional Medicine Focus</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Primary Objective</strong></td>
              <td>Diagnose acute diseases & manage acute symptoms quickly</td>
              <td>Identify root biochemical & environmental causes of dysfunction</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Diagnostic Perspective</strong></td>
              <td>Focuses on isolated organs and specialized organ compartments</td>
              <td>Examines interconnected systems (gut-brain, thyroid-adrenal, immune)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Lab Report Interpretation</strong></td>
              <td>Standard laboratory reference ranges (designed to flag acute pathology)</td>
              <td>Optimal physiological ranges, full biomarker panels & functional nutrient testing</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Primary Therapeutics</strong></td>
              <td>Pharmaceutical drugs, surgical procedures, acute therapies</td>
              <td>Therapeutic nutrition, lifestyle pacing, botanical medicine & necessary pharmaceuticals</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Patient Relationship</strong></td>
              <td>Often focused on brief, standardized clinical visits</td>
              <td>Unhurried (45–60 min) collaborative partnership mapping entire life history</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p class="table-compliance-note text-center">
        *Note: Both modalities are essential components of high-quality integrative healthcare. Dr. Harshitha Jain utilizes conventional medical diagnostics whenever indicated.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Who Benefits Most -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Candidate Profiles</span>
        <h2>Who Benefits Most from Functional Medicine?</h2>
        <p class="section-description">
          Functional medicine is especially transformative for patients in the following scenarios:
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid-3 benefits-grid">
        <div class="card benefit-card">
          <div class="benefit-number">1</div>
          <h4>“Normal” Reports, Real Symptoms</h4>
          <p>You have consulted multiple doctors and have been told your blood tests are completely normal, yet you wake up exhausted, bloated, or experiencing daily brain fog.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card benefit-card">
          <div class="benefit-number">2</div>
          <h4>Hormonal & Thyroid Complexities</h4>
          <p>You are struggling with Hashimoto’s, hypothyroidism, PCOS, PMS, or peri-menopausal symptoms that fail to respond adequately to standard single-dose pill regimens.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card benefit-card">
          <div class="benefit-number">3</div>
          <h4>Chronic Digestive Struggles</h4>
          <p>Longstanding constipation, acid reflux, severe post-meal bloating, or suspected food intolerances that keep recurring despite antacids or fiber supplements.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card benefit-card">
          <div class="benefit-number">4</div>
          <h4>Recurrent Sinusitis & Allergies</h4>
          <p>Tired of endlessly refilling anti-allergic syrups, nasal sprays, and antibiotics every few months without identifying your immune and environmental drivers.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card benefit-card">
          <div class="benefit-number">5</div>
          <h4>Chronic Stress & Sympathetic Overload</h4>
          <p>Feeling physically 'wired yet tired', having nocturnal sleep awakenings, high internal tension, and mid-afternoon energy crashes.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card benefit-card">
          <div class="benefit-number">6</div>
          <h4>Proactive Health & Longevity</h4>
          <p>Individuals who desire a comprehensive, preventative metabolic assessment to optimize their cellular health, microbiome, and longevity.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA Banner -->
  <section class="section text-center" style="background: #ffffff; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Wondering If Functional Medicine is Right for You?</h2>
      <p class="lead" style="max-width: 620px; margin: var(--space-3) auto var(--space-6);">
        Every journey begins with a conversation. Reach out to discuss your health history with Dr. Harshitha Jain.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-buttons">
        <a href="/contact#book" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Request a Consultation &rarr;</a>
        <a href="/consultation" class="btn btn-secondary btn-lg">How Consultations Work</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    background: radial-gradient(circle at 50% 50%, rgba(220, 238, 228, 0.4), transparent 60%);
    padding: var(--space-8) 0 var(--space-7);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .page-title {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  .explainer-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-7);
    align-items: center;
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .explainer-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 0.9fr;
      gap: var(--space-8);
    }
  }

  .explainer-text h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 2.5vw, 2.2rem);
    margin: var(--space-3) 0 var(--space-4);
    color: var(--color-brand-sage-dark);
  }

  .explainer-paragraphs p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .explainer-image-box {
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .explainer-img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .image-caption {
    padding: var(--space-4);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--color-slate);
    background: #ffffff;
  }

  /* Comparison Table */
  .comparison-section {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
  }

  .table-container {
    overflow-x: auto;
    padding: 0;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .comparison-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    text-align: left;
    min-width: 640px;
  }

  .comparison-table th {
    background: var(--color-brand-sage-light);
    color: var(--color-brand-sage-dark);
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-5);
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .comparison-table td {
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-5);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    vertical-align: top;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .comparison-table tbody tr:hover {
    background: var(--color-brand-sage-subtle);
  }

  .table-compliance-note {
    font-size: 0.825rem;
    color: var(--color-slate);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  /* Benefits Grid */
  .benefit-card {
    position: relative;
    padding-top: var(--space-6);
  }

  .benefit-number {
    position: absolute;
    top: var(--space-4);
    right: var(--space-4);
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    color: rgba(74, 128, 102, 0.2);
    font-weight: 300;
  }

  .benefit-card h4 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
  }

  .benefit-card p {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  .cta-buttons {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
</style>
